 "continuesQuestionOf": null,
 "segments": [
  {
   "id": "kiddushin.18a.13",
   "daf": "18a",
   "sentenceId": 12,
   "he": "וּמַפְדִּין אוֹתָהּ בְּעַל כׇּרְחוֹ. סְבַר רָבָא לְמֵימַר בְּעַל כֻּרְחֵיהּ דְּאָדוֹן. אֲמַר לֵיהּ אַבָּיֵי: מַאי נִיהוּ – דְּכָתֵבְנָא לֵיהּ שְׁטָרָא אַדְּמֶיהָ? אַמַּאי? נָקֵיט מַרְגָּנִיתָא בִּידֵיהּ, יָהֵיבְנָא לֵיהּ חַסְפָּא?",
   "en": "§ The baraita further teaches: «And one can redeem» a Hebrew maidservant «against his will. Rava thought to say» that this means «against the will of the master,» i.e., she can be redeemed even if he refuses. «Abaye said to him: What is» the mechanism for emancipating her against the will of her master? Is it «that one writes a document to him for her value,» and when she has the money she repays this debt? «Why» should it be possible to force the master to free her in this manner? He «is holding a pearl [marganita] in his hand» and «one gives him a shard» instead, as this document is currently useless."
  }
 ],
